  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The density of a monobasic strong acid (Molar mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>. The volume of its solution required for the complete neutralization of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>NaOH</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mL</mi></math> (Nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "12",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>millimole of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn></math><br />For nuetralisation, equal moles&nbsp;of monoacidic base and monobasic acid must be present:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> millimole of acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> mass of acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math></p><p>for pure acid,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac><mo>;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>/</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ml</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ml</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>ml</mi></math></p>",
